.TH AENIGMA-VPN-SERVER-HOST 8 "2026-08-17" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-vpn-server-host \- assign a static VPN IP and hostname to a client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
.B \-c
.I CLIENT_NAME
.B \-d
.I DOMAIN
.B \-i
.I IP
.B \-n
.I NETMASK
.br
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
assigns a fixed VPN address to an existing client of a VPN server instance
previously provisioned by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
by writing an
.B ifconfig-push
directive to that client's client-config-dir (ccd) file. If the server
instance has a
.B dnsmasq
hosts file configured, it also registers (or refreshes) a DNS hostname of
the form
.IB CLIENT_NAME . DOMAIN
pointing at that address, and restarts
.BR dnsmasq (8)
so the change takes effect.
.PP
This script is intended to run on the
.B VPN server
machine. It does not issue or modify any certificates; it only affects
IP assignment and, optionally, DNS resolution for an already-configured
client.
.PP
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
must be run as root, since it writes into
.I /etc/openvpn
and restarts the
.B dnsmasq
service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " CLIENT_NAME"
Name of the client to assign a static address to, e.g.
.IR john .
Used as the ccd filename and as the left-hand label of the generated
hostname. Required.
.TP
.BI \-d " DOMAIN"
Name of the VPN server instance the client belongs to (as passed to
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8)
via its
.B \-d
option). Required.
.TP
.BI \-i " IP"
Static VPN address to assign to the client, e.g.
.IR 10.8.0.10 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-n " NETMASK"
Netmask of the VPN's virtual subnet, e.g.
.IR 255.255.255.0 .
Must match the netmask the server instance was provisioned with. Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display usage information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; the client's static address was assigned (and its DNS hostname
registered or refreshed, if applicable).
.TP
.B 1
Invoked without root privileges, called with insufficient or invalid
arguments, or the target server instance's client-config-dir does not
exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB /etc/openvpn/ccd/ DOMAIN
Client-config-dir for the target server instance. Must already exist;
created by
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8).
.TP
.IB /etc/openvpn/ccd/ DOMAIN / CLIENT_NAME
Per-client ccd file. Created if it does not exist. Any existing
.B ifconfig-push
line in this file is replaced with the newly specified address; other
directives already present in the file, if any, are left untouched.
.TP
.IB /etc/openvpn/ DOMAIN /dnsmasq-hosts
Optional dnsmasq hosts file for the target server instance. If present,
an entry mapping
.IB CLIENT_NAME . DOMAIN
to
.I IP
is added or refreshed here. If absent, DNS hostname registration is
skipped with a notice, and no error is raised.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Re-running
.B aenigma-vpn-server-host
for a
.I CLIENT_NAME
that already has a static address assigned updates it in place: both the
ccd file's
.B ifconfig-push
line and, if applicable, the dnsmasq hosts entry are replaced with the
newly specified
.IR IP ,
rather than accumulating stale or duplicate entries.
.IP \(bu 2
This script does not check whether the given
.I IP
is already assigned to a different client. Assigning the same address to
two clients is not detected or prevented.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aenigma-vpn-server (8),
.BR openvpn (8),
.BR dnsmasq (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.rujas@aenigma.ro>